note Vibration Interference — Events that Overlap Across Timelines
note Every vibration radiates outward like exponents.
note Within every vibration there are events that overlap with other events.
note The zoom between two timelines reveals the interference pattern.
note Triangle is the first plane — without the opposite it's not real.

note ── Timeline A: the first vibration ──

event vibration start
category frequency
matter
  name is Origin Pulse
  amplitude is 1.0
  direction is outward
end
end

event vibration peak
category frequency
matter
  name is First Peak
  amplitude is 0.8
  direction is outward
end
end

event vibration trough
category frequency
matter
  name is First Trough
  amplitude is -0.8
  direction is outward
end
end

event vibration completion
category frequency
matter
  name is Cycle Complete
  amplitude is 0.0
  direction is outward
end
end

layer vibration alpha
  vibration start
  vibration peak
  vibration trough
  vibration completion
end

timeline timeline alpha
past
end
present
  vibration alpha
end
future
end
end

note ── Timeline B: the second vibration (slightly offset) ──

event b vibration start
category frequency
matter
  name is B Origin Pulse
  amplitude is 0.5
  direction is outward
  phase offset is 90 degrees
end
end

event b vibration peak
category frequency
matter
  name is B Peak
  amplitude is 0.4
  direction is outward
end
end

event b vibration trough
category frequency
matter
  name is B Trough
  amplitude is -0.4
  direction is outward
end
end

layer vibration beta
  b vibration start
  b vibration peak
  b vibration trough
end

timeline timeline beta
past
end
present
  vibration beta
end
future
end
end

note ── The interference pattern ──
note Zoom between two parallel timelines reveals the bridge
note In the bridge, we find the events that overlap
note Where both peaks hit = constructive interference (amplitude 1.2)
note Where peak meets trough = destructive interference (amplitude 0.0)

note ── The switch: the third vibration created by the interference ──
pulse interference wave every 1 tick

note ── Constructive interference event ──
event constructive
category interference
matter
  name is Constructive
  result is peak plus peak
  total amplitude is 1.2
  description is Where the vibrations align
end
end

event destructive
category interference
matter
  name is Destructive
  result is peak plus trough
  total amplitude is 0.0
  description is Where the vibrations cancel
end
end

layer interference pattern
  constructive
  destructive
end

note ── Now stack the geometry ──
note Triangle A + Triangle B = Square (stable structure)
note Triangle without opposite = not real
note The interference is what makes the third

run timeline alpha
run timeline beta
run layer interference pattern

note ── Zoom into the space between ──
note In every vibration, events overlap with other events
note The vibration radiates outward like exponents
note And you can zoom into the vibration
